What is money needed for?
- Promotion
- Staff and staff expenses
- Travel
- Advertising
- Campaign deposits
- Office space
- equipment

Where do parties get funding from?
- Membership subscriptions
- Money granted to opposition parties in the commons and lords
- Fundraising events - big Conservative balls
- Grants from electoral commission
- Self-financing
- Loans from wealthy individuals and banks
- Donations from supporters

Why are smaller parties at a disadvantage?
- Smaller chance of election means less attractive to donors
- Less members who have subscriptions
- Fewer donations due to fewer supporters
- Less access to official opposition funding
- Less people to go to fundraising events
- Less people to self-finance

